{"id":"mahabharata-3-225","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":225,"title":"पञ्चविंशत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 225 · Dhritarashtra hears of the Pandavas' hardship","summary":{"en":"A Brahmin tells Dhritarashtra of the Pandavas' suffering in the forest, and the king laments, fearing their revenge, especially Bhima's anger and Arjuna's weapons. Shakuni and Karna, overhearing, rouse Duryodhana with a plan.","kn":"ಕಾಡಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಪಾಂಡವರ ಕಷ್ಟವನ್ನು ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣನೊಬ್ಬನು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅವರ ಪ್ರತೀಕಾರಕ್ಕೆ, ವಿಶೇಷವಾಗಿ ಭೀಮನ ಕೋಪ ಮತ್ತು ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಅಸ್ತ್ರಗಳಿಗೆ, ಹೆದರಿ ರಾಜನು ವಿಲಪಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅದನ್ನು ಕೇಳಿದ ಶಕುನಿ ಕರ್ಣರು ಒಂದು ಯೋಜನೆಯೊಂದಿಗೆ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನನ್ನು ಪ್ರೇರೇಪಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"एक ब्राह्मण धृतराष्ट्र को वन में पाण्डवों के कष्ट बताता है, और राजा उनके प्रतिशोध से, विशेषकर भीम के क्रोध और अर्जुन के अस्त्रों से डरकर विलाप करते हैं। यह सुनकर शकुनि और कर्ण एक योजना से दुर्योधन को उकसाते हैं।","te":"అడవిలో పాండవుల కష్టాలను ఒక బ్రాహ్మణుడు ధృతరాష్ట్రునికి చెబుతాడు; వారి ప్రతీకారానికి, ముఖ్యంగా భీముని కోపానికి, అర్జునుని అస్త్రాలకు భయపడి రాజు విలపిస్తాడు. అది విన్న శకుని, కర్ణుడు ఒక పథకంతో దుర్యోధనుని ప్రేరేపిస్తారు.","ta":"காட்டில் பாண்டவர்களின் துன்பத்தை ஓர் அந்தணர் த்ருதராஷ்டிரனிடம் சொல்ல, அவர்களின் பழிவாங்கலுக்கு, குறிப்பாகப் பீமனின் சினத்துக்கும் அர்ஜுனனின் அஸ்திரங்களுக்கும் அஞ்சி மன்னன் புலம்புகிறான். இதைக் கேட்ட ஶகுனியும் கர்ணனும் ஒரு திட்டத்துடன் துரியோதனனைத் தூண்டுகிறார்கள்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവരുടെ കാട്ടിലെ ദുരിതത്തെക്കുറിച്ച് ഒരു ബ്രാഹ്മണൻ ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രനോട് പറയുന്നു; അവരുടെ പ്രതികാരത്തെ ഭയന്ന് രാജാവ് വിലപിക്കുന്നു, പ്രത്യേകിച്ച് ഭീമന്റെ കോപവും അർജുനന്റെ ആയുധങ്ങളും ഓർത്ത്. ഇത് ഒളിഞ്ഞുകേൾക്കുന്ന ശകുനിയും കർണ്ണനും ദുര്യോധനനെ ഒരു പദ്ധതിയിലൂടെ ഉണർത്തുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.225; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"घोषयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Ghoshayatra Parva (The cattle expedition)","verses":[{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवं वने वर्तमाना नराग्र्याः\nशीतोष्णवातातपकर्शिताङ्गाः ।\nसरस्तदासाद्य वनं च पुण्यं\nततः परं किमकुर्वन्त पार्थाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Parthas, best of men, living in the forest like this, their bodies worn by cold, heat, wind and sun, reached the lake and the holy forest. What did they do after that?\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"सरस्तदासाद्य तु पाण्डुपुत्रा\nजनं समुत्सृज्य विधाय चैषाम् ।\nवनानि रम्याण्यथ पर्वतांश्च\nनदीप्रदेशांश्च तदा विचेरुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Reaching the lake, the sons of Pandu sent away the crowd, arranged for them, and then wandered through lovely forests, mountains and river regions.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"तथा वने तान्वसतः प्रवीरा-\nन्स्वाध्यायवन्तश्च तपोधनाश्च ।\nअभ्याययुर्वेदविदः पुराणा-\nस्तान्पूजयामासुरथो नराग्र्याः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"As those heroes lived in the forest, ancient Veda-knowing ascetics devoted to Vedic study came to them, and those best of men honored them.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"ततः कदाचित्कुशलः कथासु\nविप्रोऽभ्यगच्छद्भुवि कौरवेयान् ।\nस तैः समेत्याथ यदृच्छयैव\nवैचित्रवीर्यं नृपमभ्यगच्छत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then one day a brahmin skilled in tales went among the Kauravas on earth. After meeting them, he chanced to go to the king, son of Vichitravirya.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"अथोपविष्टः प्रतिसत्कृतश्च\nवृद्धेन राज्ञा कुरुसत्तमेन ।\nप्रचोदितः सन्कथयां बभूव\nधर्मानिलेन्द्रप्रभवान्यमौ च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Seated and honored by the aged king, the best of the Kurus, and urged by him, he told of the sons of Dharma, Vayu and Indra, and the twins.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"कृशांश्च वातातपकर्शिताङ्गा-\nन्दुःखस्य चोग्रस्य मुखे प्रपन्नान् ।\nतां चाप्यनाथामिव वीरनाथां\nकृष्णां परिक्लेशगुणेन युक्ताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He told how thin they were, their bodies worn by wind and sun, fallen into the jaws of fierce suffering, and of Krishna, protected by heroes yet seeming unprotected, burdened with hardship.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"ततः कथां तस्य निशम्य राजा\nवैचित्रवीर्यः कृपयाभितप्तः ।\nवने स्थितान्पार्थिवपुत्रपौत्रा-\nञ्श्रुत्वा तदा दुःखनदीं प्रपन्नान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hearing his tale, King Dhritarashtra, son of Vichitravirya, was burning with pity on hearing that the king's sons and grandsons were living in the forest, fallen into a river of sorrow.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"प्रोवाच दैन्याभिहतान्तरात्मा\nनिःश्वासबाष्पोपहतः स पार्थान् ।\nवाचं कथंचित्स्थिरतामुपेत्य\nतत्सर्वमात्मप्रभवं विचिन्त्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"His heart struck with misery, choked with sighs and tears, he somehow steadied his voice and spoke of the Parthas, reflecting on what had come from himself.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"कथं नु सत्यः शुचिरार्यवृत्तो\nज्येष्ठः सुतानां मम धर्मराजः ।\nअजातशत्रुः पृथिवीतलस्थः\nशेते पुरा राङ्कवकूटशायी ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'How can Dharmaraja, the eldest of my sons, truthful, pure and noble in conduct, Ajatashatru, lie on the bare ground, he who once slept on a bed of the finest deer-skin?'\""}},{"n":10,"text":"प्रबोध्यते मागधसूतपूगै-\nर्नित्यं स्तुवद्भिः स्वयमिन्द्रकल्पः ।\nपतत्रिसंघैः स जघन्यरात्रे\nप्रबोध्यते नूनमिडातलस्थः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'He who like Indra was woken daily by bards and praise-singers from Magadha, now surely is woken at the end of the night on the ground by flocks of birds.'\""}},{"n":11,"text":"कथं नु वातातपकर्शिताङ्गो\nवृकोदरः कोपपरिप्लुताङ्गः ।\nशेते पृथिव्यामतथोचिताङ्गः\nकृष्णासमक्षं वसुधातलस्थः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'How does Vrikodara sleep, his body worn by wind and sun and swept with anger, lying in the presence of Krishna on the ground, with a body unfit for it?'\""}},{"n":12,"text":"तथार्जुनः सुकुमारो मनस्वी\nवशे स्थितो धर्मसुतस्य राज्ञः ।\nविदूयमानैरिव सर्वगात्रै-\nर्ध्रुवं न शेते वसतीरमर्षात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'And Arjuna, the gentle, high-minded one, under the sway of King Dharma's son, surely does not sleep in the huts, from resentment, all his limbs burning.'\""}},{"n":13,"text":"यमौ च कृष्णां च युधिष्ठिरं च\nभीमं च दृष्ट्वा सुखविप्रयुक्तान् ।\nविनिःश्वसन्सर्प इवोग्रतेजा\nध्रुवं न शेते वसतीरमर्षात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Seeing the twins, Krishna, Yudhishthira and Bhima deprived of comfort, he, fierce in energy, sighing like a snake, surely cannot sleep at night in the huts from anger.'\""}},{"n":14,"text":"तथा यमौ चाप्यसुखौ सुखार्हौ\nसमृद्धरूपावमरौ दिवीव ।\nप्रजागरस्थौ ध्रुवमप्रशान्तौ\nधर्मेण सत्येन च वार्यमाणौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'And the twins too, unhappy though they deserve comfort, handsome like immortals in heaven, surely lie awake, unquiet, held back by dharma and truth.'\""}},{"n":15,"text":"समीरणेनापि समो बलेन\nसमीरणस्यैव सुतो बलीयान् ।\nस धर्मपाशेन सितोग्रतेजा\nध्रुवं विनिःश्वस्य सहत्यमर्षम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'The one equal to the wind in strength, the stronger son of the wind, bound by the noose of dharma, fierce in energy, surely sighs and bears his anger.'\""}},{"n":16,"text":"स चापि भूमौ परिवर्तमानो\nवधं सुतानां मम काङ्क्षमाणः ।\nसत्येन धर्मेण च वार्यमाणः\nकालं प्रतीक्षत्यधिको रणेऽन्यैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Rolling on the ground and longing for the death of my sons, held back by truth and dharma, that champion, mightier than the others in battle, awaits the time.'\""}},{"n":17,"text":"अजातशत्रौ तु जिते निकृत्या\nदुःशासनो यत्परुषाण्यवोचत् ।\nतानि प्रविष्टानि वृकोदराङ्गं\nदहन्ति मर्माग्निरिवेन्धनानि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'When Ajatashatru was defeated by trickery, the harsh words Duhshasana said have entered Vrikodara's body and burn him like fire in firewood at a vital point.'\""}},{"n":18,"text":"न पापकं ध्यास्यति धर्मपुत्रो\nधनंजयश्चाप्यनुवर्तते तम् ।\nअरण्यवासेन विवर्धते तु\nभीमस्य कोपोऽग्निरिवानिलेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Dharma's son will not think evil, and Dhananjaya follows him. But Bhima's anger grows in the forest as fire does with the wind.'\""}},{"n":19,"text":"स तेन कोपेन विदीर्यमाणः\nकरं करेणाभिनिपीड्य वीरः ।\nविनिःश्वसत्युष्णमतीव घोरं\nदहन्निवेमान्मम पुत्रपौत्रान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Torn by that anger, the hero presses hand against hand and exhales a very terrible hot breath, as if burning these sons and grandsons of mine.'\""}},{"n":20,"text":"गाण्डीवधन्वा च वृकोदरश्च\nसंरम्भिणावन्तककालकल्पौ ।\nन शेषयेतां युधि शत्रुसेनां\nशरान्किरन्तावशनिप्रकाशान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'The wielder of the Gandiva and Vrikodara, furious, like death at the end of time, would leave no enemy army standing in battle, pouring arrows bright as thunderbolts.'\""}},{"n":21,"text":"दुर्योधनः शकुनिः सूतपुत्रो\nदुःशासनश्चापि सुमन्दचेताः ।\nमधु प्रपश्यन्ति न तु प्रपातं\nवृकोदरं चैव धनंजयं च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Duryodhana, Shakuni, the charioteer's son and Duhshasana, of very dull minds, see the honey and not the precipice, Vrikodara and Dhananjaya.'\""}},{"n":22,"text":"शुभाशुभं पुरुषः कर्म कृत्वा\nप्रतीक्षते तस्य फलं स्म कर्ता ।\nस तेन युज्यत्यवशः फलेन\nमोक्षः कथं स्यात्पुरुषस्य तस्मात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'A man, having done good or bad action, waits for its fruit as the doer. Bound to the fruit, helpless, how can he be freed from it?'\""}},{"n":23,"text":"क्षेत्रे सुकृष्टे ह्युपिते च बीजे\nदेवे च वर्षत्यृतुकालयुक्तम् ।\nन स्यात्फलं तस्य कुतः प्रसिद्धि-\nरन्यत्र दैवादिति चिन्तयामि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'When a field is well plowed and seed sown and the rain falls in season, if no fruit comes, how is it to be explained except by fate? So I think.'\""}},{"n":24,"text":"कृतं मताक्षेण यथा न साधु\nसाधुप्रवृत्तेन च पाण्डवेन ।\nमया च दुष्पुत्रवशानुगेन\nयथा कुरूणामयमन्तकालः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'As the gambler did badly, and the Pandava, who acted well, and as I, following my wicked sons, did, so this is the end-time of the Kurus.'\""}},{"n":25,"text":"ध्रुवं प्रवास्यत्यसमीरितोऽपि\nध्रुवं प्रजास्यत्युत गर्भिणी या ।\nध्रुवं दिनादौ रजनीप्रणाश-\nस्तथा क्षपादौ च दिनप्रणाशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'The wind will surely blow, even unstirred; a pregnant woman will surely give birth; night will surely follow the end of day, and the day follows night's end.'\""}},{"n":26,"text":"क्रियेत कस्मान्न परे च कुर्यु-\nर्वित्तं न दद्युः पुरुषाः कथंचित् ।\nप्राप्यार्थकालं च भवेदनर्थः\nकथं नु तत्स्यादिति तत्कुतः स्यात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Why would one act, why would others act; men would never give wealth; yet when the time for the goal has come, disaster may come: how could that be, and from where?'\""}},{"n":27,"text":"कथं न भिद्येत न च स्रवेत\nन च प्रसिच्येदिति रक्षितव्यम् ।\nअरक्ष्यमाणः शतधा विशीर्ये-\nद्ध्रुवं न नाशोऽस्ति कृतस्य लोके ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'What is guarded so that it does not break, leak or spill must be protected. Unprotected, it falls apart in a hundred pieces; surely nothing done in the world is lost.'\""}},{"n":28,"text":"गतो ह्यरण्यादपि शक्रलोकं\nधनंजयः पश्यत वीर्यमस्य ।\nअस्त्राणि दिव्यानि चतुर्विधानि\nज्ञात्वा पुनर्लोकमिमं प्रपन्नः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Dhananjaya went from the forest even to Shakra's world. See his power! Having learned the four kinds of divine weapons, he came back to this world.'\""}},{"n":29,"text":"स्वर्गं हि गत्वा सशरीर एव\nको मानुषः पुनरागन्तुमिच्छेत् ।\nअन्यत्र कालोपहताननेका-\nन्समीक्षमाणस्तु कुरून्मुमूर्षून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Who among men, having gone to heaven in his body, would wish to return, except when seeing the many Kurus struck by time and bent on dying?'\""}},{"n":30,"text":"धनुर्ग्राहश्चार्जुनः सव्यसाची\nधनुश्च तद्गाण्डिवं लोकसारम् ।\nअस्त्राणि दिव्यानि च तानि तस्य\nत्रयस्य तेजः प्रसहेत को नु ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Arjuna the left-handed archer, that Gandiva bow, essence of the world, and those divine weapons: who could withstand the energy of these three?'\""}},{"n":31,"text":"निशम्य तद्वचनं पार्थिवस्य\nदुर्योधनो रहिते सौबलश्च ।\nअबोधयत्कर्णमुपेत्य सर्वं\nस चाप्यहृष्टोऽभवदल्पचेताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hearing the king's words, Duryodhana and Saubala went off privately and told Karna everything, and he too became joyless and small-minded.\""}}]}]}